      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. to make it even more persuasive for the debate, how can i frame it so it doesn't sound like i'm just ignoring the exploitation? like, how can i argue that these systems were a necessary step for progress in those regions, almost like they were being prepared for modern civilization? i want to avoid sounding like i'm just being \"anti-colonial\" and instead focus on the idea that the transition to a modern global economy wouldn't have been possible without that initial colonial foundation.",
